  "summary": "Bind bounded owning-history authorization comparison, unresolved claim-list incompatibility and verified local Re-entry consumer landing.",
  "why": "Luis approved comparing owning authorization histories without a production cutover. Literal cases were frozen at ccd62578; tests at 52df279c pass 12 cases, with 398 neighboring regressions passing separately. Both native gates preserve bytes on the declared refusals and reconstruct permitted decisions. The same empty relied-on-claim list validates under the compiled view but fails standalone Assent; the finite profile requires it empty. The report preserves this divergence, not record-shape parity, and leaves the semantic correction to the operator. No runtime or ontology change. Separately, authorized local merge 62655e44 adds only twelve research-local Re-entry consumer files. Its sealed compatibility receipt records 650 passed and one skip; Core verified receipt/report hashes and ran 12 post-merge guards, not that full consumer suite again. Historical evidence remains unchanged. No push, release, new policy, interpreter replacement or Assent cutover.",
